senses
  entry
    definition "the act of rotating as if on an axis"
    examples ("the rotation of the dancer kept time with the music")
    id oewn-00342854-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("rotary motion")
  entry
    definition "(mathematics) a transformation in which the coordinate axes are rotated by a fixed angle about the origin"
    id oewn-13807769-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "a single complete turn (axial or orbital)"
    examples ("the plane made three rotations before it crashed" "the revolution of the earth about the sun takes one year")
    id oewn-07455579-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (revolution gyration)
  entry
    definition "a planned recurrent sequence (of crops or personnel etc.)"
    examples ("crop rotation makes a balanced demand on the fertility of the soil" "the manager had only four starting pitchers in his rotation")
    id oewn-05052532-n
    partOfSpeech n
